  "answer_text": "To prevent VoIP calls from dropping when the egress IP changes, ensure SIP/VoIP traffic uses a single, stable egress IP. Enable the Preferred IP for SIP Traffic so VoIP traffic consistently uses the same egress IP, or configure your network rule to egress to a single IP. If you truly need a fixed IP, allocate a fixed public IP to your account and bind it to the rule. Also be aware that egress IPs can change if the PoP becomes unavailable, which may cause mid-call IP changes without this configuration.",
